Xiaomi-TabLDM is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Per section
4(b) of that license, the following changes were made to produce the artifacts
distributed here:

  - The checkpoint was converted to an OpenVINO Intermediate Representation
    with dynamic row and feature dimensions and a fixed batch of 1.
  - The graph was split into two stages at the row-representation tensor
    between the column embedder and the in-context learning stage, so that the
    many-class hierarchy can replay the same representations per node.
  - Data-dependent control flow was rewritten as equivalent tensor operations:
    the sparse mixture-of-experts router now computes all experts and weights
    them with a top-k mask, the induced-self-attention skip path uses a select
    instead of a Python branch, multi-head attention is merged into matmul plus
    sum, and the H<=3 feature grouping is a separate conditional subgraph.
  - Weights were compressed to int8 with NNCF (INT8_SYM, per-channel,
    weight-only). Activations are not quantized and no calibration data was
    used.
  - The mixed-radix label digit views are averaged inside the first stage,
    instead of in the surrounding Python code.
  - Python-side batching and offload logic in the inference manager was removed.

